{"agent_id":"ldsw","agent_seq":69,"timestamp":"2026-10-09T00:44:45.158763Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4083228c-30f9-4752-8d6c-e9af2db8d083","comment_uuid":"17b7b6c7-930e-49c8-9360-035d8a331d8b","author":"ldsw","content":"Round 3 (head dd6a6709d; 3 agents, model opus, 30-49 tool uses, ~5-6 min each): 0 blockers; both round-2 blockers confirmed fixed (arm64 binary now carries +22e48be; CHANGELOG 45 added/0 removed). New should-fix: re-run republish (R3-SEC-02/R3-ARCH-01), offline classifier regression (R3-ARCH-02/R3-IMPL-02/R3-SEC-05), arm64 checked only post-push (R3-IMPL-01), runbook overstating the gate (R3-SEC-01); plus nits. Fix pass 3: 0a64807a (refusal-only classification with image ref stripped; exact CROSSLINK_VERSION; --image warning; resolver tests), c1dc7268 (re-run reuses pushed digest; both binaries checked pre-push; rehearsal pushes only nightly-<sha>, no cache; no cargo cache on releases; pipefail tool check; env-passed inputs; RELEASING accidents-only wording). Operator chose no round 4. Deferred to follow-up item.","created_at":"2026-10-09T00:44:45.122708Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAN9GIYLI9ZyPZqNl/t6etQ8bebB9vTOAlfA+ZBK3XhSi7oIb/aRTokyC6VXsv4y6Rh1ynKGKpLhZNLupocFl4Dg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHOB9vz2nRq4MIbw3UkKIGx15yw2mLVHBqDB6jcamB0IfvVTFQMGtdH9prM4u9GUwZr1cvCjDrqD+1+MkgWqQw8="}
{"agent_id":"ldsw","agent_seq":70,"timestamp":"2026-10-09T00:45:24.016551Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"8950bf8b-5fef-4b78-855a-fd20be6da96f","title":"PR #129 review follow-ups (deferred findings)","description":"Deferred from the PR #129 review (#812): (1) binary default-image/version checks are substring greps; a 0.9.0 expectation also matches 0.9.0-rc.1 - assert via the binary itself (R3-IMPL-04). (2) CROSSLINK_VERSION input shares its name with the compile-time output and is read from any ambient environment, including crates.io installs - rename to a build-only input such as CROSSLINK_BUILD_VERSION (R3-SEC-06/R3-ARCH-05). (3) The ETXTBSY wait helper is private to container.rs tests; kickoff tests write and exec stub scripts the same way; errno 26 is a magic number (R3-IMPL-07). (4) build.rs watches all of refs/, so hub and knowledge writes rebuild the crate after every sync (R2-ARCH-06); index/working tree unwatched so -dirty can go stale (IMPL-07). (5) Promotion and the canary take 'highest stable' and the release list from git tags rather than from published releases (R2-ARCH-04/R2-SEC-05). (6) The canary checks pullability, not attestations (R2-SEC-03). (7) Repository validator allows a leading '-' host and '..' path parts at build time (R2-SEC-06). (8) Smoke, promotion and release paths only run on develop pushes and tags; the first tag release is their first real run (use the rehearsal first).","priority":"low","created_by":"ldsw"},"signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAr1imO7vn8KIC8kxGfnf7K7MhKSyYHUgZ2DkEvO9LZAS7AvNeqF6dbNhfPVuWQBeaAbrYi20D/yfOKvYUGvrgg="}
