{"agent_id":"ldsw","agent_seq":93,"timestamp":"2026-10-09T01:56:27.599859Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9fac85c7-3bc8-4954-9541-e01cf6d1b395","comment_uuid":"360c76db-3d13-41fc-a649-7c0b9b0e86ed","author":"ldsw","content":"Reproduced live 2026-10-09 01:54 on this Mac: 'crosslink session work 814' failed with 'Lock confirmation timed out after 51s (threshold 30s)', session left with no active issue, yet 'crosslink locks list' showed #814 claimed by ldsw at 01:54. Retrying 'session work 814' succeeded because the lock was already ours. Same failure mode as the kickoff activation comment: the claim lands but the caller reports failure and does not record it.","created_at":"2026-10-09T01:56:27.565399Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAl9UstxOT0KxDs/YexY63+BHxHZ4vFHOTX7sttFbANsP7V/h+JMptl4/fvEhrEfCrZTcSSyvG6ujXrNUmwX7IAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOnf1I4aivJdttupUZUTmtFNn0R0qCy8MFGSzF+jGt90rMPt0OadML4cpMFtOyr2lcb+6HkjsGj57NOV2fjctwc="}
{"agent_id":"ldsw","agent_seq":94,"timestamp":"2026-10-09T01:57:23.153112Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"77c6fca8-5ce3-496c-968f-b219b70b087e","title":"Readiness blocks all work for ~30 s plus a reconcile after every wake","description":"After the Mac wakes from sleep, the readiness record is older than MAX_RECORD_AGE_SECONDS (90 s), so work-check.py blocks every Bash/Edit call until the daemon's next tick (~35 s cadence) rewrites it and a post-wake reconcile finishes. The daemon survives the sleep since upstream #107, and 'daemon ensure --wait-ready' only waits, so the block is pure latency: on a machine that idle-sleeps after one minute it lands on nearly every resumed session. Observed 2026-10-07 in mdatron and here.\n\nPossible directions for the hook design (bundled with upstream #104 / tracker #814): the daemon detects a wall-clock jump (monotonic vs wall clock, or a missed-tick gap) and refreshes immediately instead of waiting for its next tick; and/or the hook lets read-only diagnostics through while the record is merely expired with a live daemon, rather than treating expired the same as corrupt. Related: #814 (readiness windows block even diagnostics), upstream #102/#107/#111.","priority":"medium","created_by":"ldsw"},"signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCfC/6b5MH1gPsKKoStu9oHtpnIs4wl1nA+W1C2WN/wjKoAriCXR+dogU99ujGW5YeGxLOrtFm46MiXSyjyhqwE="}
{"agent_id":"ldsw","agent_seq":95,"timestamp":"2026-10-09T01:58:25.090078Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"11d3c48a-8fb6-409f-9eae-60ac56cbb3e7","comment_uuid":"91ef98f6-e0e0-49ba-926c-1cca02e4dfbb","author":"ldsw","content":"Hook design bundle (agreed 2026-10-09): upstream #104 items 2+ (not item 1, which goes with the integration-drift bundle: #105, #13, #15, #20, #99), upstream #116 agent hook policy (needs dollspace's policy decision), and tracker #816 post-wake readiness block.","created_at":"2026-10-09T01:58:25.055220Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAEbaCbB4hBONSlRMzES/f5bVYNMrnlkxCOBWeuvZpqjUlwAqQPFsqpYTquPLBeVZi5CYRPFFHyfWJw0yggI4rBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMM/0ptrsaJVkalxIIzxGzJvw4IKoaK+zgzoKxRf4tSLNiYgBNX9es6H+HLgINMOOBznWFqOxbocgZ5ln2elyAY="}
{"agent_id":"ldsw","agent_seq":96,"timestamp":"2026-10-09T01:59:16.682189Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"eb1a4388-3986-477b-b657-86a21e83c800","title":"Design: write-path cost and lock-confirmation semantics (upstream #118, #110, #120)","description":"Design bundle agreed 2026-10-09. Upstream #118: one write spawns ~350-615 git processes; lock confirmation takes 34-57 s locally and 58-86 s downstream against a 30 s bound; heartbeats and readiness ride the same slow path. Upstream #110: a lock claim that times out lands anyway, so the lock is stranded and the caller does not record it (kickoff activation path in launch.rs; reproduced again 2026-10-09 with 'session work 814'). Upstream #120 / tracker #807: nothing creates or refreshes the knowledge cache; the fix belongs in daemon activation and its tick, which this design changes. Output: a /design document covering write cost, confirmation semantics (landed-after-timeout), kickoff failure cleanup, heartbeat/readiness off the slow path, and knowledge-cache housekeeping.","priority":"high","created_by":"ldsw"},"signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA9FT8tlWYal9EeRm4tAaXz3AR2wmGIXv25Vb25vQ7qhD3f2SmrbBWX/c7ueNtaSpcS/lhzCB8dYNQwXCsAXvQU="}
