{"agent_id":"ldsw","agent_seq":98,"timestamp":"2026-10-09T02:08:18.702774Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2426f9e3-80d4-424d-92a9-21e9255e9f06","title":"v3 hubs cannot steal or force-release another agent's lock","description":"Found while designing #817 (2026-10-09), from code; not yet reproduced by a failing test. apply_lock_event (crosslink/src/compaction.rs:1075) ignores LockClaimed and LockReleased from any agent other than the current holder. steal_lock_v2 and force_release_lock_v2 (crosslink/src/shared_writer/locks.rs:89-133) first run clear_stale_lock_state, which edits the file checkpoint, events.log and locks/ under cache_dir, but a v3 reduce reads the checkpoint ref (RefHubSource::read_checkpoint, hub_source.rs:534) and replays agent refs, so the edits have no effect: steal returns Contended, force-release publishes a LockReleased the reducer drops. auto_steal_if_configured ignores the claim result (lock_check.rs:106). tests/smoke/coordination.rs test_adversarial_stale_lock_steal_audit passes either way (its else branch accepts a failed steal; its assertion matches 'Locked' for agent A). Consistent with the ~35 dashboard-bootstrap locks from May 2026 still listed STALE on the shared hub. Kickoff cleanup (upstream #110 item 2) depends on a working release path for another agent's lock. Fix designed in #817.","priority":"high","created_by":"ldsw"},"signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQM3GIt2usl/I8YxtRg7HNmr8P3ljdSr1KGRFdJjRpUyPuB22ziUroJFM9JK9FD4B8u/H2/1bVu/dZwBsQCAtVQc="}
