{"agent_id":"ldsw","agent_seq":104,"timestamp":"2026-10-09T03:05:29.824750Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e3ff54f1-396b-445f-8677-339ac0ae5b03","title":"Dead kickoff agents leave identities, host key files and trust approvals behind","description":"From the #817 design review, 2026-10-08. init_worktree_agent (crosslink/src/commands/kickoff/launch.rs) creates an agent identity with its private key on the host (.crosslink/keys/<agent>_ed25519, commands/agent.rs) and commits a host-signed trust approval to the hub (commands/trust.rs). Kickoff undo and cleanup (increment 1 of .design/write-path-cost.md) leave all three in place deliberately: revoking the approval with 'crosslink trust revoke' would leave the agent's already-published events signed by a revoked key. Needs a design for retiring a dead agent's key and approval without invalidating its published history (for example, marking it retired rather than revoked).","priority":"low","created_by":"ldsw"},"signed_by":"SHA256:2DlhR+oFnVKNEPsahz+cG6GYEUUTKJkJUtdRSniweHI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgDPj6fD8/zRZvUXWw//OEuKiIM7V2BnG7lBF86x/hrWIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQICuubLv8oi+F8LAN/oHqZOJD+0jfgLrtC3p/g8y1+tglkLjSyAyktxpDb5HacCSOqaiWjkAok5aSVkhQ+XHCgo="}
